IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oas-core-pension`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part I, "Amount of Pension": the partial pension's share of the full pension (ss 3(3) to 3(5)),
-- the full monthly pension and its quarterly adjustment (s 7), the increase at 75 (ss 7(5), 7.1(5), 7.1(6)) and the
-- increase for putting off the application (s 7.1).
--
-- THE THREE AMOUNTS (NOTES.md, "Cross-references out of my ranges" and the keel's register, item 10). The Act speaks of
-- three different full monthly pensions, and piece oa2 takes them as inputs under the keel's exact names:
--   V1  `the amount of the full monthly pension calculated without regard to subsection 7(5)`: the amount per ss 7(1) to (4).
--       The text gives only the January 1, 1985 figure; every later quarter is the quarter before times a ratio of
--       published indices (s 7(2)), so the figure for a given month is an INPUT here, and `s 7(2)-(4): the quarterly adjustment`
--       is the step that produces it from the quarter before.
--   V2  `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)`:
--       V1 with the 10% increase at 75 (s 7(5)). This is the rule `s 7(5): ...` below.
--   V3  `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)`: what is actually payable. This is the rule
--       `s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` below.
-- Rounding: the Act rounds nothing except the aggregate period (s 3(4)). The Regulations round the products (Regs 7
-- and 8, piece oa3), so every amount here is exact.

§ `Amount of Pension`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 7(1): the basic amount

-- src:153 | Amount of Pension
-- src:154 | Basic amount of full pension
-- src:155 | 7 (1) The amount of the full monthly pension that may be paid to any person for a month in the payment quarter commencing on January 1, 1985 is two hundred and seventy-three dollars and eighty cents.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7(1) (src:153-155)
`s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension for a month in the payment quarter commencing on January 1, 1985` MEANS 273.80

-- The text states that one figure only. For a month before that payment quarter the text states none, and for a month after
-- it the figure is not stated either: it is worked from the quarter before by s 7(2). Both give NOTHING here.
-- src:155 | 7 (1) The amount of the full monthly pension that may be paid to any person for a month in the payment quarter commencing on January 1, 1985 is two hundred and seventy-three dollars and eighty cents.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7(1) (src:155)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension stated for the month` month MEANS
    IF (`the payment quarter containing the month containing` month)'s `first day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1985 1 1)
    THEN JUST (`s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension for a month in the payment quarter commencing on January 1, 1985`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment of the full monthly pension

-- What one quarter's adjustment leaves behind for the next: the amount for the quarter, and, where paragraph 7(4)(b)
-- is holding the adjustment back, the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter of the quarter that began the hold.
-- src:156 | Quarterly adjustment of basic amount of full pension
-- src:157 | (2) Where a full monthly pension has been authorized to be paid to a person, the amount of the pension shall be adjusted quarterly, in such manner as may be prescribed by regulation, so that the amount that may be paid to that person for a month in any payment quarter commencing after March 31, 1985 is the amount obtained by multiplying
-- src:158 | (a) the amount of the pension that might have been paid to that person for a month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter
-- src:159 | by
-- src:160 | (b) the ratio that the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter bears to the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter.
-- src:161 | No decrease in amount of full pension
-- src:162 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the amount of a full monthly pension that may be paid to a pensioner for any month in a payment quarter shall be not less than the amount of the full monthly pension that was or may be paid to a pensioner for any month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter.
-- src:163 | Effect of reduction in Consumer Price Index
-- src:164 | (4) Where, in relation to any payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter is lower than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter,
-- src:165 | (a) no pension adjustment shall be made pursuant to subsection (2) in respect of that payment quarter; and
-- src:166 | (b) no pension adjustment shall be made pursuant to that subsection in respect of any subsequent payment quarter until, in relation to a subsequent payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter is higher than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in paragraph (a), in which case the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in that paragraph shall be deemed to be the second adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, ss 7(2), 7(3), 7(4) (src:156-166)
DECLARE `s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment` HAS
    `the amount that may be paid for a month in the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
    `the Consumer Price Index carried forward under paragraph 7(4)(b)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- The step from the quarter before to the quarter in question. The two indices are the register inputs (the Regulations'
-- Regs 9 rounding of the average is piece oa3's, so they are taken as the Regs give them); the product is not rounded
-- (Regs 8 is piece oa3's too). A quarter must commence after March 31, 1985 for s 7(2) to apply; otherwise NOTHING.
--   no hold in force:  the index for the first adjustment quarter LOWER than the second: no adjustment (7(4)(a)), and
--                      the second index is carried forward as the base (7(4)(b));
--                      otherwise the amount before times the ratio first : second (7(2)).
--   a hold in force:   the carried base stands in for the second index (7(4)(b), "deemed to be the second adjustment
--                      quarter"); no adjustment until the first index is HIGHER than that base, then the amount before
--                      times the ratio first : base, and the hold ends.
-- 7(3): the amount is never less than the amount in the three-month period before.
-- src:157 | (2) Where a full monthly pension has been authorized to be paid to a person, the amount of the pension shall be adjusted quarterly, in such manner as may be prescribed by regulation, so that the amount that may be paid to that person for a month in any payment quarter commencing after March 31, 1985 is the amount obtained by multiplying
-- src:158 | (a) the amount of the pension that might have been paid to that person for a month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter
-- src:159 | by
-- src:160 | (b) the ratio that the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter bears to the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter.
-- src:161 | No decrease in amount of full pension
-- src:162 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the amount of a full monthly pension that may be paid to a pensioner for any month in a payment quarter shall be not less than the amount of the full monthly pension that was or may be paid to a pensioner for any month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter.
-- src:163 | Effect of reduction in Consumer Price Index
-- src:164 | (4) Where, in relation to any payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter is lower than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter,
-- src:165 | (a) no pension adjustment shall be made pursuant to subsection (2) in respect of that payment quarter; and
-- src:166 | (b) no pension adjustment shall be made pursuant to that subsection in respect of any subsequent payment quarter until, in relation to a subsequent payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter is higher than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in paragraph (a), in which case the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in that paragraph shall be deemed to be the second adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, ss 7(2), 7(3), 7(4) (src:157-166)
GIVEN `the first day of the payment quarter` IS A DATE
      `the amount of the pension that might have been paid to that person for a month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: section 2 (piece oas-g0): "Consumer Price Index", "first adjustment quarter"; section 9 (piece oa3): Regulations, the average
      `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: section 2 (piece oas-g0): "second adjustment quarter"; section 9 (piece oa3): Regulations, the average
      `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index carried forward from an earlier payment quarter under paragraph 7(4)(b)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment`
`s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` `the first day of the payment quarter` `the amount of the pension that might have been paid to that person for a month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index carried forward from an earlier payment quarter under paragraph 7(4)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the payment quarter` AT MOST (YearMonthDay 1985 3 31)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment` WITH
                   `the amount that may be paid for a month in the payment quarter` IS
                       max `the amount of the pension that might have been paid to that person for a month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter`
                           (IF withheld
                            THEN `the amount of the pension that might have been paid to that person for a month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter`
                            ELSE `the amount of the pension that might have been paid to that person for a month in the three month period immediately before that payment quarter`
                                   TIMES (`the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` DIVIDED BY base))
                   `the Consumer Price Index carried forward under paragraph 7(4)(b)` IS
                       IF withheld THEN JUST base ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        -- 7(4)(b): after a fall, the second index of the quarter that began the hold is deemed to be the second index of this quarter
        base MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Consumer Price Index carried forward from an earlier payment quarter under paragraph 7(4)(b)`
            WHEN JUST carried THEN carried
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`
        -- 7(4)(a): lower than the second; 7(4)(b): not yet higher than the carried base
        withheld MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Consumer Price Index carried forward from an earlier payment quarter under paragraph 7(4)(b)`
            WHEN JUST carried THEN NOT (`the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` GREATER THAN carried)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` LESS THAN `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 7(5): the increase at 75, which is V2

-- "Beginning in the payment quarter commencing on July 1, 2022, for the period that begins in the month after the month in
-- which a person attains 75 years of age, the amount ... is increased by 10%." The amount to increase is the one the caller
-- passes: s 7(5) passes V1, s 7.1(5) the amount as increased under 7.1(1), s 7.1(6) the partial amount as increased under 7.1(2).
-- src:167 | Full monthly pension — persons aged 75 years or older
-- src:168 | (5) Beginning in the payment quarter commencing on July 1, 2022, for the period that begins in the month after the month in which a person attains 75 years of age, the amount of the full monthly pension, as it is calculated in accordance with subsections (1) to (4), is increased by 10%.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7(5) (src:167-168)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      birth IS A DATE
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` month birth amount MEANS
    IF     (`the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1))
       AND (`the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST (`the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` (`the day on which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 75)))
    THEN amount TIMES (1 PLUS 10%)
    ELSE amount

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 3(3), 3(4), 3(5): the partial pension

-- src:112 | Rounding of aggregate period
-- src:113 | (4) For the purpose of calculating the amount of a partial monthly pension under subsection (3), the aggregate period described in that subsection shall be rounded to the lower multiple of a year when it is not a multiple of a year.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(4) (src:112-113)
GIVEN `the aggregate period, in years, that the applicant has resided in Canada after attaining 18 years of age and before the day on which the application is approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 3(4): the aggregate period rounded to the lower multiple of a year` `the aggregate period, in years, that the applicant has resided in Canada after attaining 18 years of age and before the day on which the application is approved` MEANS
    FLOOR `the aggregate period, in years, that the applicant has resided in Canada after attaining 18 years of age and before the day on which the application is approved`

-- "the amount of a partial monthly pension, for any month, shall bear the same relation to the amount of the full monthly
-- pension for that month as the aggregate period ... determined in accordance with subsection (4), bears to 40 years."
-- "The amount of the full monthly pension" is V2 by s 2.1(1): the core's `the amount of a full monthly pension` picks it from
-- the amount before and the amount after any increase under 7.1(1) or (2). "Subject to subsection 7.1(3)": see that rule.
-- src:110 | Amount of partial pension
-- src:111 | (3) Subject to subsection 7.1(3), the amount of a partial monthly pension, for any month, shall bear the same relation to the amount of the full monthly pension for that month as the aggregate period that the applicant has resided in Canada after attaining 18 years of age and before the day on which the application is approved, determined in accordance with subsection (4), bears to 40 years.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(3) (src:110-111)
GIVEN `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate period, in years, that the applicant has resided in Canada after attaining 18 years of age and before the day on which the application is approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 3(3): the amount of a partial monthly pension` `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the aggregate period, in years, that the applicant has resided in Canada after attaining 18 years of age and before the day on which the application is approved` MEANS
    (`the amount of a full monthly pension` `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)`)
        TIMES ((`s 3(4): the aggregate period rounded to the lower multiple of a year` `the aggregate period, in years, that the applicant has resided in Canada after attaining 18 years of age and before the day on which the application is approved`) DIVIDED BY 40)

-- "may not be increased on the basis of subsequent periods of residence": a period of residence that begins on or after the day
-- of approval of a partial pension does not raise the amount (the aggregate in 3(3) stops at "before the day on which the
-- application is approved"). A period that began before that day is not "subsequent" (fork OA1-F24 of NOTES.md).
-- src:114 | Additional residence irrelevant for partial pensioner
-- src:115 | (5) Once a person’s application for a partial monthly pension has been approved, the amount of monthly pension payable to that person under this Part may not be increased on the basis of subsequent periods of residence in Canada.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(5) (src:114-115)
GIVEN `the person's application for a partial monthly pension has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the period of residence in Canada` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(5): the amount of monthly pension payable may be increased on the basis of the period of residence` `the person's application for a partial monthly pension has been approved` `the first day of the period of residence in Canada` `the day on which the application was approved` MEANS
    NOT (    `the person's application for a partial monthly pension has been approved`
         AND `the first day of the period of residence in Canada` AT LEAST `the day on which the application was approved`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 7.1: putting off the application

-- s 7.1(4): the months that count. The period runs from the month after the month the person becomes qualified to the month
-- of approval; no month counts before July 2013 (a), after the month in which the person attains 70 (b), or if the pension
-- would not be paid by 5(3) or would be suspended under 9(1) or (3) were the person a pensioner (c). (a) and (b) are applied
-- to the ends of the period; (c) is a count the person states (fork OA1-F6 of NOTES.md).
-- src:178 | Limitation
-- src:179 | (4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), the amount of a pension is not increased for any month
-- src:180 | (a) before July 2013;
-- src:181 | (b) after the month in which the person attains 70 years of age; or
-- src:182 | (c) in which the person’s pension would not be paid by virtue of subsection 5(3), or would be suspended under subsection 9(1) or (3), if the person were a pensioner.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7.1(4) (src:178-182)
GIVEN `the day on which the person becomes qualified to receive the pension` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person's application is approved` IS A DATE
      birth IS A DATE
      `the number of those months in which the pension would not be paid by virtue of subsection 5(3), or would be suspended under subsection 9(1) or (3), if the person were a pensioner` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7.1(4): the number of months for which the pension is increased` `the day on which the person becomes qualified to receive the pension` `the day on which the person's application is approved` birth `the number of those months in which the pension would not be paid by virtue of subsection 5(3), or would be suspended under subsection 9(1) or (3), if the person were a pensioner` MEANS
    max 0 (monthsInPeriod MINUS `the number of those months in which the pension would not be paid by virtue of subsection 5(3), or would be suspended under subsection 9(1) or (3), if the person were a pensioner`)
    WHERE
        -- the period begins in the month after the month in which the person becomes qualified; 7.1(4)(a): not before July 2013
        firstMonth MEANS
            IF `the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the day on which the person becomes qualified to receive the pension` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 2013 7 1)
            THEN `the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the day on which the person becomes qualified to receive the pension`
            ELSE YearMonthDay 2013 7 1
        -- the period ends in the month in which the application is approved; 7.1(4)(b): not after the month in which the person attains 70
        lastMonth MEANS
            IF `the first day of the month containing` `the day on which the person's application is approved` AT MOST (`the month in which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 70)
            THEN `the first day of the month containing` `the day on which the person's application is approved`
            ELSE `the month in which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 70
        monthsInPeriod MEANS
            IF lastMonth AT LEAST firstMonth
            THEN (`the number of months from the month containing` firstMonth `to the month containing` lastMonth) PLUS 1
            ELSE 0

-- s 7.1(1): "increased by 0.6% for each month": the amount per ss 7(1) to (4) (V1) plus 0.6% of it for each counted month.
-- src:169 | Voluntary deferral — full monthly pension
-- src:170 | 7.1 (1) If a person applies for their pension after they become qualified to receive a full monthly pension, the amount of that pension, as it is calculated in accordance with subsections 7(1) to (4), is increased by 0.6% for each month in the period that begins in the month after the month in which the person becomes qualified for that pension and that ends in the month in which the person’s application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7.1(1) (src:169-170)
GIVEN `the amount of the full monthly pension calculated without regard to subsection 7(5)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months for which the pension is increased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7.1(1): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased` `the amount of the full monthly pension calculated without regard to subsection 7(5)` `the number of months for which the pension is increased` MEANS
    `the amount of the full monthly pension calculated without regard to subsection 7(5)` TIMES (1 PLUS (0.6% TIMES `the number of months for which the pension is increased`))

-- s 7.1(2): the partial pension "as it is calculated in accordance with subsection 3(3) without regard to subsection 7(5), at
-- the time that they become qualified", plus 0.6% of it for each counted month.
-- src:171 | Voluntary deferral — partial monthly pension
-- src:172 | (2) If a person applies for their pension after they become qualified to receive a partial monthly pension, the amount of that pension, as it is calculated in accordance with subsection 3(3) without regard to subsection 7(5), at the time that they become qualified for that pension, is increased by 0.6% for each month in the period that begins in the month after that time and that ends in the month in which the person’s application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7.1(2) (src:171-172)
GIVEN `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is calculated in accordance with subsection 3(3) without regard to subsection 7(5), at the time that the person becomes qualified` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months for which the pension is increased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7.1(2): the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased` `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is calculated in accordance with subsection 3(3) without regard to subsection 7(5), at the time that the person becomes qualified` `the number of months for which the pension is increased` MEANS
    `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is calculated in accordance with subsection 3(3) without regard to subsection 7(5), at the time that the person becomes qualified` TIMES (1 PLUS (0.6% TIMES `the number of months for which the pension is increased`))

-- s 7.1(5) and (6): the same increase of 10% at 75, applied to the full amount as increased under (1), and to the partial
-- amount as increased under (2). One relation, written once in s 7(5) above; each provision has its own name here.
-- src:183 | Full monthly pension — persons aged 75 years or older
-- src:184 | (5) Beginning in the payment quarter commencing on July 1, 2022, for the period that begins in the month after the month in which a person attains 75 years of age, the amount of the full monthly pension, as it is increased under subsection (1), is increased by 10%.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7.1(5) (src:183-184)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      birth IS A DATE
      `the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7.1(5): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1) and increased by 10% at 75` month birth `the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1)` MEANS
    `s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` month birth `the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1)`

-- src:185 | Partial monthly pension — persons aged 75 years or older
-- src:186 | (6) Beginning in the payment quarter commencing on July 1, 2022, for the period that begins in the month after the month in which a person attains 75 years of age, the amount of the partial monthly pension, as it is increased under subsection (2), is increased by 10%.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7.1(6) (src:185-186)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      birth IS A DATE
      `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7.1(6): the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2) and increased by 10% at 75` month birth `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2)` MEANS
    `s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` month birth `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2)`

-- s 7.1(3): the greatest of the three amounts, "unless they decide otherwise". What the person receives when they decide
-- otherwise is not stated, and neither is the amount of a person who is qualified for no pension (fork OA1-F7): NOTHING.
-- The caller passes each amount with the increase at 75 already applied (the increase multiplies every candidate alike
-- from the same date, so the greatest is the same either way).
-- src:173 | Greatest amount of pension
-- src:174 | (3) A person who is qualified to receive a monthly pension shall, unless they decide otherwise, receive the greatest of the following amounts:
-- src:175 | (a) the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1), if the person is qualified to receive a full monthly pension,
-- src:176 | (b) the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2), and
-- src:177 | (c) the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is calculated under subsection 3(3) at the time that the person’s application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7.1(3) (src:173-177)
GIVEN `the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1), if the person is qualified to receive a full monthly pension` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is calculated under subsection 3(3) at the time that the person's application is approved` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the person decides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` `the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1), if the person is qualified to receive a full monthly pension` `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2)` `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is calculated under subsection 3(3) at the time that the person's application is approved` `the person decides otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the person decides otherwise` OR null candidates
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (maximum candidates)
    WHERE
        candidates MEANS
            append (`oa1: a possible amount as a list of none or one` `the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1), if the person is qualified to receive a full monthly pension`)
              (append (`oa1: a possible amount as a list of none or one` `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2)`)
                      (`oa1: a possible amount as a list of none or one` `the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is calculated under subsection 3(3) at the time that the person's application is approved`))

-- A helper for the rule above: the amount as a list of none or one.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 7.1(3)
GIVEN amount IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`oa1: a possible amount as a list of none or one` amount MEANS
    CONSIDER amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST x THEN LIST x
